{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Third-Party IdP Sign-In Failures",
	"Description": "Sign-in through a federated identity provider failed. The interesting failure reasons are the ones about validating the SAML response or matching the transformed username: replayed assertions, a mismatched signing key, or a username mapping that no longer lines up all look like this, and so does an adversary probing a federation they only partly control.\n\nEvent types: user.authentication.auth_via_IDP, user.authentication.auth_via_inbound_SAML, user.authentication.auth_via_inbound_delauth, user.authentication.auth_via_social\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_okta_sign_in_events_via_third_party_idp/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_okta_sign_in_events_via_third_party_idp.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "81f2c0a8-59b1-5924-aeab-06cda692d6b2",
